<title>USA: ComEd Zion 1 Ill. nuke cuts power -- NRC.</title>
<headline>ComEd Zion 1 Ill. nuke cuts power -- NRC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Edison Co's 1,040 megawatt Zion nuclear power unit 1 in Zion, Ill., reduced output to 70 percent of capacity as of early Tuesday, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>In its daily plant status report for Tuesday, the NRC said Zion 1 was &quot;ramping power down,&quot; but gave no reason for the production cut.</p>
<p>A Commonwealth Edison spokesman was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Commonwealth Edison is a subsidiary of Unicom Corp.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
</text>
